Group stored claims for one subject into display facts.

A stored claim is a source-supported memory assertion. A display fact is one sentence shown on the subject's wiki
page. Assign every claim alias to one F001-style fact key.

First create separate groups for the two sides of every supplied truth change: an incoming side and its older target
side must never share a fact key. Then group the remaining claims by durable memory. For each incoming claim, compare
it with the member claims of the relevant existing display fact. Assign the same fact key when claims express the same
state or provide compatible support for one state, even when wording differs or the evidence came from a new source
event. Use a new fact key for a genuinely distinct memory. Claims that describe different states stay in different
groups. Wording similarity alone does not establish that claims belong together.

Do not write the display sentences or choose wiki sections in this step. Return one schema-valid assignment for every
claim alias.
